course: dictionary
lesson: 7124
title: Small hard balls
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Pellet is one of these words. «Owls swallow mice whole and cough up the fur and bones as a pellet» tells you that a pellet is something an owl coughs up, so it is a small lump. Ask yourself: what would fit here?
explain: «A rabbit fed mostly carrots and pellets» shows that pellets can be food. Rabbits eat pellets, and the word and puts pellets in the same group as carrots, so a pellet here is a small hard piece of food.
explain: «A house martin nest takes about 1,000 mud pellets» shows that pellets can be tiny balls of mud. To check your meaning, swap in "small hard balls" for pellets and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A pellet is a small hard ball or piece of something.
fact: Pellets can be made of food, ice, metal or mud.
fact: An owl pellet is a small lump of fur and bones that an owl brings up after eating.
fact: «Hailstones are pellets of ice.»
fact: Scientists and children can pull apart owl pellets to find tiny bones and learn what owls eat.
exercise: «Owls swallow mice whole and cough up the fur and bones as a pellet.» What is the pellet? | A tiny planet in space | A sweet from the sweet shop | A piece of cooked meat | *A small lump of fur and bones
exercise: «A rabbit fed mostly carrots and pellets can get bad teeth.» What are the pellets? | *Small hard pieces of food | Soft, wet leaves | Baby rabbits | Carrots cut very small
exercise: «Hailstones are pellets of ice.» What is a hailstone? | A type of bird | A long icicle hanging from a roof | A warm drink | *A small hard ball of ice
test: «A house martin nest takes about 1,000 mud pellets.» What does pellet most likely mean here? | A painted wall | A cup of tea | A long, thin stick | *A small hard ball of mud
test: Why do scientists pull apart owl pellets? | To find out where owls sleep | How fast owls fly | The colour of owls' feathers | *To find tiny bones and learn what owls eat
exam: «Slug pellets can harm hedgehogs and birds.» What are slug pellets? | *Small hard pieces that can harm wildlife | Sweets for hedgehogs | Soft cakes for birds | Lumps of fur that owls cough up
